  "title": "BigLake Views Gain IAM, 'resource' Parameter Now Required",
  "summary": "BigLake now offers full IAM policy management for Views with new `getIamPolicy`, `setIamPolicy`, and `testIamPermissions` methods. Heads up: The `resource` parameter is now strictly required across the API, which is a breaking change.",
  "details": "Developers can now programmatically manage access control for BigLake Views using the newly added `projects.catalogs.namespaces.views.getIamPolicy`, `setIamPolicy`, and `testIamPermissions` methods. These methods enable granular permission management for your views. Crucially, the `resource` parameter has been made strictly required. Any existing API calls that previously omitted or treated `resource` as optional will now fail and must be updated to explicitly provide this parameter.",
